# Gapless fast path, part 4 of 6: hook the load-start 80 ms delay.
name: gapless-4-delay-hook
kind: module
module: 33
region: code
address: 0x03088fea
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: The stock load-start routine (0x03088d9c) ends its audio
  re-arm sequence with delay_ms(80) at 0x03088fea, after the I2S and
  DMA configuration for the new track. The patch redirects that single
  BL to the delay cave at 0x030514fe (0023) in resident module 0 --
  cross-module branches are routine in this firmware (module 33 itself
  calls module 0 throughout). The cave preserves the call contract
  exactly: it either tail-calls the stock delay_ms with the same r0
  and lr, or (fast path, same rate only) returns at once. No other
  delay_ms call site is touched; in particular the delay_ms(100) at
  0x03089f16 in codec open needs no cut -- disassembly shows it sits
  before the DAC-guard branch at 0x03089e52, so it already runs only
  on the first open of a session, never on a natural advance.
expect: dbf7abfc
replace: c8f788fa
